IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei2-nouns`
IMPORT `ei2-work-sharing-and-courses`
IMPORT `ei2-disqualification`

-- Tests of ei2-disqualification (ss 27 and 28). Expected values are written by hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`an opportunities measure, s 59(b)` MEANS JUST `ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support`
`an assistance services measure, s 59(c)` MEANS JUST `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services`
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
`no measure` MEANS NOTHING

§ `s 27(1)(a) to (d)`

-- (a) "has not applied for a suitable employment that is vacant ... or has failed to accept the employment after it has been offered"
#ASSERT `s 27(1)(a) not applying for or accepting a suitable employment` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(1)(a) not applying for or accepting a suitable employment` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1)(a) not applying for or accepting a suitable employment` FALSE FALSE
-- (b)
#ASSERT `s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment` FALSE
-- (c) all three: a direction given, not carried out, and reasonable
#ASSERT `s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- "if the direction was reasonable ...": an unreasonable direction disqualifies nobody.
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- (d) directed, purpose (i) only, not attended
#ASSERT `s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- purpose (ii) only
#ASSERT `s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- neither purpose stated in (i) or (ii)
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- attended
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- not directed
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `s 27(1) - the whole sentence, with the good-cause gate`

#ASSERT `s 27(1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under Part I` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under Part I` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under Part I` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under Part I` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- None of (a) to (d).
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under Part I` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- With good cause (the gate is "without good cause"): not disqualified even though (a) holds.
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under Part I` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `s 27(1.1) - termination of a referral`

-- (a) referred with agreement, assistance under a measure of 59(b): other than one referred to in 59(c).
#ASSERT `s 27(1.1)(a) a referral with the claimant's agreement to an activity assisted under a measure other than one in paragraph 59(c)` TRUE `an opportunities measure, s 59(b)`
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1.1)(a) a referral with the claimant's agreement to an activity assisted under a measure other than one in paragraph 59(c)` TRUE `an assistance services measure, s 59(c)`
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1.1)(a) a referral with the claimant's agreement to an activity assisted under a measure other than one in paragraph 59(c)` TRUE `no measure`
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1.1)(a) a referral with the claimant's agreement to an activity assisted under a measure other than one in paragraph 59(c)` FALSE `an opportunities measure, s 59(b)`
-- (b) terminated; (i) not attended without good cause AND the Commission's opinion that completion is unlikely
#ASSERT `s 27(1.1)(b) the Commission has terminated the referral for one of the stated reasons` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- (i) is a conjunction: without the opinion it fails
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1.1)(b) the Commission has terminated the referral for one of the stated reasons` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (ii) withdrew without good cause
#ASSERT `s 27(1.1)(b) the Commission has terminated the referral for one of the stated reasons` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- (iii) expelled
#ASSERT `s 27(1.1)(b) the Commission has terminated the referral for one of the stated reasons` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- referral not terminated by the Commission
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1.1)(b) the Commission has terminated the referral for one of the stated reasons` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- (a) and (b) together
#ASSERT `s 27(1.1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under Part I` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1.1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under Part I` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(1.1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under Part I` FALSE TRUE

§ `s 28(1) - the number of weeks`

-- "(a) ... 27(1)(a) or (b) shall be not fewer than 7 or more than 12"
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment` EQUALS JUST 7
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment` EQUALS JUST 7
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the most weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the most weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment` EQUALS 12
-- "(b) ... 27(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 27(1.1) shall be not more than 6": no least number is stated.
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1.1) referral to a course, program or activity terminated` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the most weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the most weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the most weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1.1) referral to a course, program or activity terminated` EQUALS 6
-- Boundaries on each side of 7 and 12 for (a).
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(1) the number of weeks determined is within the limits of the Act` `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment` 6
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the number of weeks determined is within the limits of the Act` `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment` 7
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the number of weeks determined is within the limits of the Act` `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment` 12
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(1) the number of weeks determined is within the limits of the Act` `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment` 13
-- (b) the same limits.
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the number of weeks determined is within the limits of the Act` `ei2 s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment` 9
-- Boundaries for (c): at most 6, with no floor.
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the number of weeks determined is within the limits of the Act` `ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` 6
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(1) the number of weeks determined is within the limits of the Act` `ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` 7
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the number of weeks determined is within the limits of the Act` `ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` 0
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the number of weeks determined is within the limits of the Act` `ei2 s 27(1.1) referral to a course, program or activity terminated` 1
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(1) the number of weeks determined is within the limits of the Act` `ei2 s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission` 12

§ `s 28(2), (5) - serving the weeks`

-- 5 weeks of disqualification; the week is the 1st, 5th, 6th, 0th week of the run; not deferred.
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the week is served as a week of disqualification` 5 1 FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the week is served as a week of disqualification` 5 5 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(2) the week is served as a week of disqualification` 5 6 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(2) the week is served as a week of disqualification` 5 0 FALSE
-- Deferred under (5): not served.
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(2) the week is served as a week of disqualification` 5 1 TRUE
-- (5) "otherwise entitled to special benefits or benefits by virtue of section 25"
-- entitled to benefits for a reason other than the regular one (here pregnancy): special benefits
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the serving of the disqualification is deferred` TRUE `pregnancy` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the serving of the disqualification is deferred` TRUE `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` FALSE
-- entitled to regular benefits only: not special benefits, so no deferral
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(5) the serving of the disqualification is deferred` TRUE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` FALSE
-- benefits by virtue of section 25
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the serving of the disqualification is deferred` FALSE `pregnancy` TRUE
-- not otherwise entitled to any benefits (the reason given is then beside the point)
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(5) the serving of the disqualification is deferred` FALSE `pregnancy` FALSE

§ `s 28(3), (4) - carried forward`

-- (4) "700 or more hours": 699 does not stop the carry-forward, 700 does.
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(4) no weeks of disqualification are carried forward` 699
#ASSERT `s 28(4) no weeks of disqualification are carried forward` 700
#ASSERT `s 28(4) no weeks of disqualification are carried forward` 701
-- (3) "within two years after the event": event 15 March 2025.
#ASSERT `s 28(3) a benefit period is established within two years after the event` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(3) a benefit period is established within two years after the event` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 16)
#ASSERT `s 28(3) a benefit period is established within two years after the event` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(3) a benefit period is established within two years after the event` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 14)
-- An event on a leap day: the second anniversary is 28 February 2026 (the keel clamps; fork F4).
#ASSERT `s 28(3) a benefit period is established within two years after the event` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(3) a benefit period is established within two years after the event` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
-- 4 weeks unserved, a later benefit period within two years, 699 hours: all 4 are carried forward.
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the weeks of disqualification carried forward into the later benefit period` 4 (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) 699 EQUALS 4
-- 700 hours: none.
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the weeks of disqualification carried forward into the later benefit period` 4 (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) 700 EQUALS 0
-- The later benefit period is established more than two years after: none.
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the weeks of disqualification carried forward into the later benefit period` 4 (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 16) 0 EQUALS 0
-- Nothing unserved.
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the weeks of disqualification carried forward into the later benefit period` 0 (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) 0 EQUALS 0

§ `s 28(6) and (7)`

#ASSERT `s 28(6) benefits are deemed to be paid for the week` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(6) benefits are deemed to be paid for the week` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(7) the deeming of benefits as paid is no bar to the request` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(7) the deeming of benefits as paid is no bar to the request` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(7) the deeming of benefits as paid is no bar to the request` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(7) the deeming of benefits as paid is no bar to the request` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
